              ],
              [
                "8",
                "8",
                "[9]"
              ],
              [
                "9",
                "9",
                "[] (done)"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The BFS order is 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9."
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "Differentiate between DFS and BFS (short question 8). Long question 7(b): give the BFS order from A for the exercise graph.",
            "explanation": "DFS uses a stack (or recursion) and goes deep along one branch before backtracking; BFS uses a queue and visits all nodes at one level before the next, finding shortest paths in unweighted graphs. Both take O(V + E) time. For the exercise graph BFS from A gives A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I."
          },
